# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows' default `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites the
# working tree to CRLF on checkout. The suite pins Swift and JavaScript
# invariants by matching against the source text itself (test/macos/
# launcher_test.exs), so a checkout that silently changes the bytes turns
# multi-line patterns into failures that reproduce nowhere else.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch files are the exception: cmd.exe is the one interpreter here that is
# not reliably LF-tolerant, and CRLF is what the Windows checkout already
# produced for them.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never touch, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.torrent binary
